er_parity namespace."],"finding":"The plan states its reference inventories were produced by a string-based 'tree-wide per-symbol sweep' / re-measured citations rather than by symbol-graph lookup (find_referencing_symbols). This is the stated-method defect the rubric flags: a complete sweep result is luck, not structural proof, and the plan leans on it for load-bearing exact counts (12 vs 11 _attach_code_review_metrics call sites, two vs three shadow_compare tests). A dynamic/string reference (monkeypatch.setattr, getattr, module-attribute access such as test_provider_parity.py:374's pp.verdict_decision) is exactly what a grep sweep over-captures or an LSP-only pass misses, so neither half alone is a sound derivation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f68e9f304164dd119","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context/Problem paragraph ('Every citation was re-measured on origin/main...enumerated tree-wide, not sampled') and Testing ('Re-run the tree-wide per-symbol sweep before trusting the greps below')","norm_id":"n4cb7ba3ce3ef9e52","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A string-sweep over-counts/undercounts a symbol whose only reference is dynamic (getattr/monkeypatch.setattr/importlib) — e.g. a monkeypatch.setattr(fse, 'prerequisite_packing_spot_eval', ...) style attribute reference that structural tools surface but a name-grep could miscategorize, or vice-versa.","If the sweep missed a module-attribute consumer like test_provider_parity.py:374's pp.verdict_decision, the rename would leave an unpatched caller."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"no","no_existing_mitiga